    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm working with a client who's been stuck at the same weight on their back squat for like 4 weeks now. they're hitting everything else fine but the squat just isn't moving. how do deload weeks or changing up the volume help get past a plateau like this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Deload weeks allow your central nervous system and muscles to fully recover from accumulated fatigue, which can break through staleby points where the deadlift is stuck. Altering volume by shifting to higher reps or fatiguing movements stimulates different muscle adaptations without erasing progress. Investigating biomechanical limitations, such as ankle mobility or squat depth, is also crucial when specific velocity drops are the only bottleneck. Consistency in technique combined with these strategic adjustments often restarts the linear progression.",
      "source": "target",
